# Every path is served by the SPA, which then decides what to render.
#
# Without this Netlify looks for a real file at the requested path and shows
# its own 404 — so /ca/, /blogs, /events/kids-club and every other deep link
# breaks on a hard refresh or when entered directly, even though they work
# when you navigate to them from the home page.
#
# 200, not 301: the URL has to stay as it was, because the router reads the
# country out of it (see The country is in the URL in CLAUDE.md).
/*    /index.html   200
